.TITLE "brew"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
The missing package manager for macOS. Homebrew installs the __packages__ you need
that Apple did not include by default. It manages __binaries__, __libraries__,
and __applications__ within their own sandboxed directories. It simplifies
the installation and management of open-source software on macOS.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**homebrew**

.DIV "TLDR"
**brew install __formula__**
Installs a specific package or formula (e.g., __node__, __git__).
> __formula__: The name of the package to install.

**brew uninstall __formula__**
Removes an installed formula from the system.
> __formula__: The name of the package to uninstall.

**brew update**
Fetches the newest versions of Homebrew and all formulae from GitHub.
> 

**brew upgrade**
Installs newer versions of all currently installed packages.
> 

**brew search __text__**
Searches for available formulae matching the provided __text__.
> __text__: The search term.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
`brew` is an essential tool for any macOS developer or power user. Regularly
running `brew cleanup` helps remove old versions of installed formulae and
free up disk space. Always run `brew doctor` if you encounter unexpected
errors after an installation.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:softwareupdate**

